# Editing JES entities
@scenario tutorial_lesson_25
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code shy]
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/panel.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt indicator]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: The JES panel contains separate entities for its background, indicator and title. This lets you resize one element without moving the others.
ginger: Open {b}scripts/scenes/panel.jes{/b}. In the indicator entity, change the Panel2D width and height from 28 to 42.
ginger: Open the example panel. The indicator should grow in place. If the background grew instead, check the entity name above the edited component.
ginger: Next change only its fill. Compare the colour and size independently. Press Enter or Esc to return.
ginger: Read the braces as ownership. The indicator entity contains a Panel2D component. Its x and y locate the panel, w and h size it, and fill supplies its colour.
ginger: Changing 28 to 42 adds 14 units per side. The area changes from 784 to 1,764 square units, so a 50 percent increase in each dimension produces 2.25 times the area.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Open the example panel -> visit_panel
> Work out the indicator's new area -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: Which edit affects only the indicator?
> Edit the named indicator entity. -> correct
> Tint the entire stage. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: A stage tint applies more widely. Find the entity that owns the indicator's dimensions and fill.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Change the component inside the named indicator entity. The panel background and title keep their own settings.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_25]
[flag tutorial_done_25]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_5]
[end]

@label visit_panel
[jes push scripts/scenes/panel.jes label check]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/panel.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt indicator]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Change only w from 28 to 42 in the indicator component. Leave h at 28. Predict a wider rectangle and verify it in the running JES panel.
ginger: Then change h to 42 as well. Compare the square with the original using its upper-left edge as a reference. Keeping x and y fixed anchors that edge while the opposite edges move.
ginger: If the square needs to keep its original centre, compensate for the 14-unit growth. Subtract seven from x and seven from y, then compare the centre before and after the edit.
ginger: Undo the size changes and alter a single fill channel. If the entire background changes, check the enclosing entity name before changing the numeric values again.
@label practice_question
ginger: With size changing from 28 to 42, what keeps the same centre for a top-left anchored panel?
> Subtract 7 from x and y. -> practice_result
> Subtract 14 from x and y. -> practice_hint
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Subtracting the full growth moves the centre seven units too far. Compare the old and new half-sizes.
[jump practice_question]
@label practice_result
ginger: The centre sits half a width and half a height from the origin. The half-size grew by seven, so the origin moves back by seven.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the exercise again -> practice
> Back to topics -> return_hub
